/-!
# Coefficient rings of a local ring

Let `(R, 𝔪)` be a local ring. A subring `Λ ⊆ R` is a *coefficient ring* of `R` when `Λ` is a
complete local ring whose maximal ideal is `Λ ∩ 𝔪`, the residue field of `Λ` maps isomorphically
onto the residue field of `R`, and `Λ ∩ 𝔪 = pΛ`, where `p` is the characteristic of the residue
field of `R`. Here *complete* means complete and separated for the maximal-ideal-adic topology,
that is, `Λ → lim_n Λ/𝔪_Λ^n` is an isomorphism, and no Noetherian hypothesis is imposed.

The three conditions leave exactly three possibilities. If `p = 0`, that is if `R` contains a
field, then `Λ ∩ 𝔪 = 0`, so `Λ` is a field mapping isomorphically onto `R/𝔪`. If `p > 0` and no
power of `p` vanishes in `R`, then `Λ` is a complete discrete valuation ring with uniformizer `p`,
that is a Cohen ring. If `p > 0` and `p^n = 0` in `R` for some `n`, then `Λ` is an Artinian local
ring with maximal ideal `(p)` and residue field `R/𝔪`. The Cohen structure theorem (Stacks 032A)
asserts that every complete local ring has a coefficient ring, and this is the notion in which that
theorem is phrased.

## Main definitions

* `LocalSubring.IsCoefficientRing`: the predicate on a local subring `Λ` of a local ring `R` saying
  that `Λ` is a coefficient ring of `R`.

## Implementation notes

The Stacks Project states the definition for a complete local ring `(R, 𝔪)`, but none of the
conditions uses completeness of `R`, so it is not assumed here.

All the ideals, residue fields and characteristics are those of `Λ` and of `R` themselves: `Λ ∩ 𝔪`
is the contraction `(maximalIdeal R).comap Λ.toSubring.subtype` of `𝔪` along the inclusion, an
ideal of `Λ`, and `pΛ` is the ideal of `Λ` generated by the image of `p` in `Λ`, not the ideal of
`R` it generates. The characteristic is read off the residue field of `R`; by the third field it
agrees with the characteristic of the residue field of `Λ`. It is allowed to be `0`, in which case
the last condition reads `Λ ∩ 𝔪 = 0`, the equicharacteristic case above.

The map of residue fields is `IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map Λ.toSubring.subtype`, the map induced by
the inclusion, which is available because of the first field. Requiring it to be surjective is
requiring it to be an isomorphism, injectivity of a ring homomorphism out of a field being
automatic (`RingHom.injective`).

The subring is a term of Mathlib's `LocalSubring R`, which bundles a subring with the statement
that it is a local ring, so that the locality of `Λ` is carried by the type. The remaining part of
the first condition, that the maximal ideal of `Λ` is `Λ ∩ 𝔪`, is `IsLocalHom Λ.toSubring.subtype`
by `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_comap`.

## References

* [StacksProject 0326](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0326), Definition 10.160.4
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]

/-- A *coefficient ring* of a local ring `(R, 𝔪)` is a local subring `Λ ⊆ R` such that `Λ` is
complete with maximal ideal `Λ ∩ 𝔪`, the residue field of `Λ` maps isomorphically onto the
residue field of `R`, and `Λ ∩ 𝔪 = pΛ`, where `p` is the characteristic of the residue field
of `R`. -/
@[stacks 0326]
public structure LocalSubring.IsCoefficientRing (Λ : LocalSubring R) : Prop where
  /-- The inclusion `Λ → R` is local, i.e. the maximal ideal of `Λ` is `Λ ∩ 𝔪`. -/
  isLocalHom : IsLocalHom Λ.toSubring.subtype
  /-- `Λ` is complete and separated for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, i.e. the canonical map
  `Λ → lim_n Λ/𝔪_Λ^n` is an isomorphism. -/
  isAdicComplete : IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal Λ.toSubring) Λ.toSubring
  /-- The residue field of `Λ` maps isomorphically onto the residue field of `R`; the map is the
  one induced by the inclusion, and surjectivity is all that is asked, a ring homomorphism out of
  a field being injective. -/
  residueField_map_surjective :
    letI := isLocalHom
    Function.Surjective (ResidueField.map Λ.toSubring.subtype)
  /-- `Λ ∩ 𝔪 = pΛ`, where `p` is the characteristic of the residue field of `R`. -/
  comap_maximalIdeal_eq_span_ringChar :
    (maximalIdeal R).comap Λ.toSubring.subtype
      = Ideal.span {(ringChar (ResidueField R) : Λ.toSubring)}
